  "definition": "A disorder is an abnormal condition of the body or mind that leads to discomfort, impaired functioning, or distress for the affected person or people around them. The term is often used broadly for problems such as injuries, disabilities, syndromes, symptoms, unusual behaviors, or atypical bodily or mental functioning.",
